irect salespeople. It operates in Europe, Asia Pacific, South America, and the Middle East. ESAB Corporation was founded in 1904 and is headquartered in North Bethesda, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Shyam P. Kambeyanda | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $276K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["ESAB Corporation is a mid-cap industrials business with a $4.6B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $213M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 58% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5791127238662406},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has